Example 1 (KY Ex. 4.3):
  D_2 point (Fraction(1, 2), Fraction(0, 1)) : hand case split (n <= 8: |2nd coord diff| = 1/n >= 1/8 ; n >= 9: 1st coord diff >= 1/6 ) gives distance to B_2 >= 1/8
  numerical check: min over n <= 10^5 of the distance to b_n = 0.187885 (>= 1/8)
  distance to the limit point (1,0) = 1/2 > 0; so d not in cl(B_2); sigma = 1/2 > 0
  KY prove in Ex. 4.3 that c = (1,1) is NOT generated -> printed Cor. 3.12 fails
  KY's proof uses 2d/sigma(d) = (Fraction(2, 1), Fraction(0, 1)) ; the segment (0, 2d/sigma) contains (1,0) in cl(B_2), so Prop. 3.11(ii) fails for it
Example 2 (sfree Prop. 2(b)):
  D_2 point (Fraction(1, 2), Fraction(0, 1)) : q = 5/4 > 0 (not in B, so not in cl(B_2)); sigma = 1/2 > 0
  D_2 point (Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(1, 2)) : q = 1/4 > 0 (not in B, so not in cl(B_2)); sigma = 1/2 > 0
  s = 1/10 : q(-s^2, 1-s) = -1/10000 = -s^4 : True (points of B_2 -> (0,1))
  s = 1/1000 : q(-s^2, 1-s) = -1/1000000000000 = -s^4 : True (points of B_2 -> (0,1))
  first point of B on ray e_2: q(0,t) = (1-t)^2 vanishes only at t = 1 -> (0,1) in cl(B_2),
  so in the corrected reading ray e_2 needs D_1 = {(0,1)} with sigma = 1 (not > 1): corrected Cor. 3.12 does not apply, consistent with Prop. 2(b)
